title: Proposition 94
---
order: 94
---
short_label: X.94
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If an area is contained by a rational straight line and a fourth apotome, then the side of the area is minor.
----
proof:

Let the area be contained by the rational straight line {AC} and the fourth apotome {AD}.

I say that the side of the area {AB} is minor.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="410" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.94 diagram" src="propX94.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the area AB (ACBD) on the rational AC and the fourth
    // apotome AD, with the annex DG, E bisecting DG, F from the application
    // to AG, the parallels EH, FI, GK, the rectangles DFIB and IFGK, and the
    // squares LM (RMPL) and NO (PNQO) about the diameter PR, with SQ, TQ and
    // the gnomon arc UVW.
    // Added, all hidden at rest: solid twins FI, GK (initiallyHidden) so the
    // parallels stroke down from F and G; transparent segment targets
    // (;0;0;0); faceless twins ABh, LM, NO of the filled ACBD, RMPL, PNQO,
    // since a lit filled square would be raised over NO and the lines inside
    // it (#140); faceless targets AI, FK, DH, EK, DK, AK, the rectangles MN
    // (N,P,M,T) and LO (L,P,O,S), the square ST (R,S,Q,T), and the gnomon
    // UVWg (L,P,M,T,Q,S), reached as {UVW|UVWg} because the arc owns UVW;
    // a right-angle marker angLPM for "the angle LPM", the corner of the
